   <property name="text">
    <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here is the milling stage in which the malt is crushed inside the mill in order to break open the grain husks. This increases the surface area of the malt, which will be usefull in the mashing step. This is due to the increased surface area allowing more efficient sugar extraction.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This process turns the malt into what is called grist. The level of milling is very important, as too little milling results in poor sugar extraction, while over-milling can lead to a thick, difficult to process mash. The level of milling also is very important as it has a high effect of the alcohol potential of the beer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
   </property>
